WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.268
-Welcome back.
I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.404
I know you're
at "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:07.773
and that's how you first
know me, right?

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:09.509
From "Saturday Night Live."
-Did you hear about that?

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.677
-No.
-So, okay, listen.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.780
When I was growing up --
I mean, I am 17,

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:19.685
but when I was like...
Really, like 5 or 4

00:00:19.685 --> 00:00:22.355
or more or 3 -- I don't know.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:25.058
I used to watch a show called
"The Electric Company,"

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:29.229
and -- [ Laughs ]
There was a guy on it,

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:33.199
and he had eyeliner,
and he was singing about H's

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:36.135
'cause it was, like,
a little kids show,

00:00:36.135 --> 00:00:39.205
and he was like --
the hook was like --

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.274
What is it?
It was like "My H's," like...

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:44.077
Something, something, nothing --
I don't even know what it was,

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:47.113
but it was you, and then
I remember seeing you on TV,

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:48.781
and I was like,
"That's the guy

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:50.450
from the commercial
with the H's."

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.252
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:54.720
-It's such a long career.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.923
-I got a pocket full of H's, and
I'm not afraid to use them.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.091
-Yeah, pocket full of H's.
It was like a Ramones

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:59.659
type of song.
-And it was you!

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.862
-♪ I got a pocket full of H's,
and I'm not afraid to use them ♪

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:05.298
But no one saw that
in my whole lifetime.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:07.100
[ Laughter ]
-But I thought --

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.969
-I made movies, I was on
"Saturday Night Live" for years.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.937
"Weekend Update" -- hello!

00:01:11.937 --> 00:01:16.009
-So, like, when I was on
this show, like, a while ago...

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:17.744
-You didn't know me from
"Saturday Night Live"?

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.146
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.281
-That's what I heard
that you did.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.581
-I was so excited
to meet you because...

00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:24.350
-That's hilarious.
They all told me

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.651
that you knew me from --
you got a story

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:27.487
about "Saturday Night Live."
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.355
I can't believe you saw that.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.423
Oh, my God.
No one saw that.

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:31.690
And I was, like --
I was pulling H's

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.159
out of my pocket
and throwing them and stuff.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.094
-Yeah, you were.
You had thick eyeliner.

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:37.997
-Let's talk about you.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.966
-Let's talk about your music
right here.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:43.102
Look at this -- "When We Fall
Asleep, Where Do We Go"

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:45.371
is the biggest selling
debut album in a decade.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.839
You're the first
female artist --

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:48.908
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.977
You're the first female artist

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:53.513
to have 14
simultaneous chart entries.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:57.483
Your music and videos have been
streamed 15 billion times.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:59.652
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:02.088
That's you!
That's you I'm talking about.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.824
I got to say,
the album is so great.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:07.159
Everyone loves it.
Your fans are young,

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:09.195
they're old,
they're all sorts of people.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.063
Why do you think
this music resonates

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:12.531
with so many different people?

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:16.568
-Um...I mean, it was, like,
a big goal,

00:02:16.568 --> 00:02:19.005
so I feel like I'm --
I don't know why necessarily.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.973
I just think
I'm mainly happy about it.

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:23.442
I think, like, I grew up
listening to so much

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:27.046
different kind of music,
like, old stuff and new stuff

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:31.050
and hip-hop and contemporary
and then jazz and Peggy Lee,

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.952
Frank Sinatra and then
Tyler the Creator

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:35.822
and, like, Nas.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:38.557
-I was all over the place,
and I think I just put it

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:39.925
into my music.

00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:41.427
And with the album,
specifically,

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.596
there was one thing
I really tried to do,

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:46.131
which was that --
There are like 14 songs

00:02:46.131 --> 00:02:48.468
on the album,
and one of the goals I had

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:51.804
was I wanted to make an album
that I could put

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:56.909
14 people into a room that each
had, like, fully different,

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:59.345
fully different tastes --
like, one person like this,

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.580
one person like this,
and that's all they liked,

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:03.515
and that
if I played them my album,

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:06.019
each person would like
at least one song.

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:09.322
-Wow. That's a really cool way
of attacking it.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:10.856
And you did it.
I mean, I heard it.

00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:13.258
I think I heard "Bad Guy" first,
and I was like,

00:03:13.258 --> 00:03:15.961
"I don't know if anyone's ready
for this type of music."

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:17.730
It was so different.
I was like --

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.065
-I didn't, either.
I thought they'd hate it.

00:03:20.065 --> 00:03:22.068
-I didn't know why.
I was like, "Is this..."

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:24.637
Dude, you changed the face
of pop music

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.039
and music, in general, 'cause
we were hearing the same song

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:29.175
for the last three years,
and you just played something

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:32.044
totally different, like, pwkk!
And I was like --

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:34.446
Now we're gonna hear
nothing but songs like "Bad Guy"

00:03:34.446 --> 00:03:36.482
for the next three years.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.117
Because that's all --
It was good.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.452
-Thank you so much.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.153
-I love the whole record.
-That's really sweet.

00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:42.522
-Which one --
Just tell me,

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.890
which one do you think
would go to me out of these 14?

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:47.026
-Would go to you?
-Yeah. What number am I?

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:49.661
-What number are you?
-Yeah, in this album.

00:03:49.661 --> 00:03:51.196
-Oh.
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:51.196 --> 00:03:53.732
-I mean, you just made it pretty
clear that you're "Bad Guy."

00:03:53.732 --> 00:03:56.169
[ Laughter ]
So 2.

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:57.970
-It was a trick question.
Yeah, you're right.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.238
I like that.
But I'm a good guy.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:00.672
-You are a good guy.
-Thank you, yeah.

00:04:00.672 --> 00:04:02.541
-A good bad guy.
-I am, yeah.

00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:04.810
-I want to talk about this thing
happening right here.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:05.978
-Yes, sir.
-What's going on?

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:08.114
You sprained your ankle,
or what's happening?

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.882
-Look at my little sock.
-Yeah.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.685
-Um, yeah, I sprained this.
You know, what's funny

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.520
is they're actually
both sprained.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.889
This is like --
-What?

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:19.025
-Three weeks old,
four weeks old.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.760
This one is like two months old.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.429
Hilarious.
-How do you -- how did you --

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:24.797
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:25.998
But how did you sprain
your ankle,

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:27.499
and how do you perform
with a sprained ankle?

00:04:27.499 --> 00:04:30.169
-I just wear this, and I pretend
it's not sprained.

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:31.503
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.503 --> 00:04:34.640
I sprained it in the lawn
like 3 seconds into the show.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.510
For real. Like, I walked
on stage and sprained it.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.246
-Walking?
How hard do you walk?

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:42.548
-I jumped. One leg --
-There you go.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:45.218
-It was the sixth count
into "Bad Guy."

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:48.120
It was, like,
literally the sixth count --

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:51.090
♪ Bum, ba da da,
buh buh -- ♪

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.592
-And that's where you did it.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.893
-Why?
You stood up.

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:55.294
You really stood up.
-I was ready to get into it.

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:56.696
I was ready to jump.
-You was about to jump.

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:57.863
-I was ready to jump,
and that's it.

00:04:57.863 --> 00:04:59.665
Now I sprained my ankle
just now.

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:01.567
I just sprained --
I sprained both of my ankles.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:02.668
-It wasn't only
just embarrassing

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:03.802
that I sprained it.

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:05.071
It was more embarrassing
that I, like, fell.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.772
You know what I'm saying?
Who falls, you know?

00:05:06.772 --> 00:05:08.040
[ Laughter ]
Embarrassing.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.141
-You didn't tell me you fell.

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:10.743
So, you went for it,
and then you fell.

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.845
But did people think
it was part of the dance?

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.547
-Probably.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:16.882
Or they just were like,
"Pfft! She fell."

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:18.751
Like, that's
what I was worried about,

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.319
that they were like,
"Loser, she fell."

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:22.521
-No.
-But, really, I was, like,

00:05:22.521 --> 00:05:24.257
laying there in agonizing pain.

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:26.959
Thing is, I have sprained
this leg -- or, this ankle

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:30.163
like five times before,
so I knew exactly what it was.

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:32.131
-Maybe you're wearing
the wrong footwear.

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:33.465
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.465 --> 00:05:35.701
-I actually was wearing --
That's crazy you say that.

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:38.237
I was wearing a pair of shoes
I had never performed in.

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:39.505
-You got to bring me
on tour with you.

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.640
-Yeah, I do.
I do!

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.342
-Talk about the new world tour.

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:45.211
Can you believe
you're going on a world tour,

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:47.279
Billie Eilish, 17 years old?

00:05:47.279 --> 00:05:48.614
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:51.684
That's what I'm talking about!
That's how you do it!

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:52.818
But you're doing
something different

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:53.919
and cool with this tour.

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:55.988
Talk about
the green part of this tour.

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:59.625
-Yes. Well, basically,
we just announced today,

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:02.895
as you just said, it's the
Where Do We Go World Tour.

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:04.697
-The Where Do We Go World Tour.
-Where Do We Go World Tour.

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:07.133
And, basically,
we're trying to be

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:09.968
as, like, green as possible
on the entire tour.

00:06:09.968 --> 00:06:12.304
So, there's, like --
We're actually bringing someone

00:06:12.304 --> 00:06:17.443
from Reverb, this company
that basically specializes --

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:18.610
Is that a word?
-Yeah.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:21.847
-Okay.
-"Reverb" or "specializes"?

00:06:21.847 --> 00:06:23.315
-Specializes.
-Specializes.

00:06:23.315 --> 00:06:24.550
Reverb, I'd be like,
"Oh, is that...?"

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:28.588
Yeah, but Reverb.
-Specializes in, like,

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:31.858
the best and most healthy and
green ways to do everything.

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:34.493
So there's
no plastic straws allowed,

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:36.962
the fans are gonna
bring their own water bottles,

00:06:36.962 --> 00:06:39.398
there's gonna be
recycle cans everywhere.

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:41.334
'Cause it's like,
if something's recyclable,

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.369
it doesn't matter unless
there's a recycle bin, you know?

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:45.237
It doesn't do anything
unless there is one.

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:47.106
-Don't want just
recycled trash everywhere.

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:48.641
You're actually
gonna recycle everything.

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:50.909
-Yeah.
-I love that you're doing this.

00:06:50.909 --> 00:06:52.511
You're doing
so many great things.

00:06:52.511 --> 00:06:54.013
I love it.
-Thank you.

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:58.484
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:02.021
I'm psyched to have you back.
Come back whenever you want.

00:07:02.021 --> 00:07:04.090
Do we know what songs
you're doing on "SNL"?

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:06.092
Can you say, or...?
-Ooh!

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:07.726
-I actually haven't said,
but I can say.

00:07:07.726 --> 00:07:09.395
-You can?
-I don't know if I can.

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:11.397
-Why not, right?
What songs you gonna do?

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:13.832
-This is live.
-Yeah, we're too late.

00:07:13.832 --> 00:07:15.368
-A little too late.

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:16.835
You know what?
I don't care, so why not?

00:07:16.835 --> 00:07:19.571
I'm doing "Bad Guy"
and "I Love You."

00:07:19.571 --> 00:07:21.240
-Oh, my gosh!
Come on.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:25.077
So watch that Saturday!
Billie Eilish tomorrow night.

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:26.679
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:28.380
"When We All Fall Asleep,
Where Do We Go"

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:30.383
is available now!

00:07:30.383 --> 00:07:31.850
Yeah, give her
a standing ovation. Why not?

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:33.986
You can watch Billie perform
on the season premiere

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:36.621
of "Saturday Night Live"
tomorrow night,

00:07:36.621 --> 00:07:39.058
at 11:30 p.m., on NBC.

